1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,615
Hello, it's DiGi. And here's Pebble.

2
00:00:05,415 --> 00:00:08,690
Grown up, come and sit close.

3
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:14,110
This one is about bedtime, and it is a cosy one.

4
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,844
Let's breathe together.

5
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:24,582
Breathe in, and blow out slowly, like cooling a cup of warm milk.

6
00:00:25,382 --> 00:00:28,951
One more. In. And out. Lovely.

7
00:00:30,301 --> 00:00:34,249
Today's special words are wind down.

8
00:00:35,049 --> 00:00:40,681
Winding down is the slow, quiet bit before sleep.

9
00:00:40,681 --> 00:00:46,887
Like a toy that slows down, and slows down, and stops.

10
00:00:48,237 --> 00:00:51,744
When you sleep, your body gets the rest it needs.

11
00:00:52,544 --> 00:00:58,747
That is why everybody needs sleep. Grown ups too. And Pebble.

12
00:00:58,747 --> 00:01:00,679
Pebble needs a lot.

13
00:01:02,029 --> 00:01:08,000
Screens are fun. They are bright, and busy, and exciting.

14
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:13,064
And exciting things make it hard for your brain to wind down.

15
00:01:13,064 --> 00:01:15,230
Even when you are really tired.

16
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:22,810
Pause me here, and ask each other the question. I'll wait.

17
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:30,470
So here is our bedtime rule. Ready?

18
00:01:31,270 --> 00:01:34,064
Screens go to bed first.

19
00:01:35,414 --> 00:01:40,926
The tablet goes to its own bed. Not in your bedroom.

20
00:01:40,926 --> 00:01:43,046
In its special spot.

21
00:01:43,846 --> 00:01:47,753
And look. The grown up's phone goes to bed too.

22
00:01:47,753 --> 00:01:50,829
Screens go to bed first. Everybody's.

23
00:01:52,179 --> 00:01:56,187
Oh, Pebble. The book does not go to bed.

24
00:01:57,537 --> 00:02:01,777
The book comes with us. Books are for bedtime.

25
00:02:03,127 --> 00:02:09,045
Then it's time for three cosy things. Teeth. Story. Cuddle.

26
00:02:10,395 --> 00:02:14,181
Your three cosy things might be different.

27
00:02:14,181 --> 00:02:17,606
A song, a bath, a chat about your day.

28
00:02:17,606 --> 00:02:20,401
You and your grown up can pick.

29
00:02:21,751 --> 00:02:27,979
Pause me here, and choose your three together. Take your time.

30
00:02:32,429 --> 00:02:39,174
Sometimes, at bedtime, something you saw on a screen gets stuck in your head.

31
00:02:39,974 --> 00:02:44,036
If that happens, you can always tell your grown up.

32
00:02:44,036 --> 00:02:45,469
Even in the night.

33
00:02:46,819 --> 00:02:49,002
You will never be in trouble for telling.

34
00:02:50,352 --> 00:02:56,566
Let's practise. Grown up, you say: it's nearly bedtime.

35
00:02:57,366 --> 00:03:02,790
And then the little one answers: screens go to bed first.

36
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:06,895
Let's try it now. Pause me if you need to.

37
00:03:08,245 --> 00:03:13,982
So. We wind down before sleep. Screens go to bed first.

38
00:03:13,982 --> 00:03:16,486
Then, three cosy things.

39
00:03:17,836 --> 00:03:24,769
Tonight, put the tablet to bed in its spot, and do your three cosy things.

40
00:03:26,119 --> 00:03:31,255
Goodnight, Pebble. Goodbye from DiGi. See you next time.
